.TH "AGENT-SKILLS" "7" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
agent-skills \- index of bundled Codex and Antigravity task skills
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Debian development image bundles task-specific instructions for
coding agents. Each skill has its own SKILL.md with canonical workflow,
requirements, safety constraints and examples. This page is a short
human-readable discovery index, NOT a replacement for the skill files.
.PP
The list below represents skills in the repository source. A running
container may contain an older published image, local user edits or
additional skills from outside this repository. Verify the actual
agent environment before assuming a skill is available.
.SH BUNDLED SKILLS
.SS "g2-overlay"
Gentoo overlay tooling: inspect, lint and verify ebuilds, Manifests,
USE flags, caches and overlay structure. Prefer narrow read-only
checks before using any mutation or repair operations.
.SS "gh-address-comments"
Address actionable GitHub PR review threads and conversation comments,
using gh and the bundled fetch_comments.py helper. Keep review-thread
resolution tied to verified fixes.
.SS "gh-fix-ci"
Inspect failing GitHub Actions PR checks and logs using gh and the
bundled inspect_pr_checks.py helper; distinguish diagnosis-only
requests from requests to change code.
.SS "gosubc"
Generate, inspect, validate and format Go command declarations,
export templates, produce man pages and manage skills through the
gosubc CLI. Verify the installed generator revision before using
flags or modifying generated code.
.SS "header-metadata"
Inspect, lint and verify website metadata with the header CLI,
including OpenGraph, Twitter metadata, canonical references,
redirects, linked images and social-card generation.
.SS "playwright"
Browser automation with the installed playwright-cli: open pages,
take snapshots, interact with current element references, capture
screenshots and traces, and reproduce interface regressions.
.SS "rntocase-safe"
Safely preview and apply batch filename-case transformations with
rntocase. Inspect dry runs and collisions before changing files.
.SS "txtar-project"
Operate arran4/txtar to inspect, generate, extract and modify
TXTAR fixtures. Distinguish its subcommand interface from the
unrelated golang.org/x/exp/cmd/txtar executable.
.SH INSTALLATION AND AUTHORITATIVE SOURCES
The source catalog is under:
.PP
.nf
containers/dev-dotfiles-debian/agent-skills/<name>/SKILL.md
.fi
.PP
The container Dockerfile copies bundled skills into Codex's
image-managed directory:
.PP
.nf
/etc/codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
.fi
.PP
It also copies the catalog to
/usr/local/share/dev-dotfiles-debian/agent-skills, from which
dev-dotfiles-sync-agent-skills refreshes Antigravity's user-scoped
skills at:
.PP
.nf
~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
.fi
.PP
The Antigravity sync keeps user-edited or unrelated skills intact,
using per-skill content fingerprints stored in
~/.local/state/dev-dotfiles-debian/managed-skills. Skills removed
from the image are not deleted automatically from persistent homes.
Codex's image-owned skills change when the container image is
rebuilt and relaunched, not merely when the Git repository is edited.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man agent-skills
find /etc/codex/skills -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md
find "$HOME/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills" \
  -maxdepth 2 -name SKILL.md
less /etc/codex/skills/g2-overlay/SKILL.md
less "$HOME/.gemini/antigravity-cli/skills/g2-overlay/SKILL.md"
dev-dotfiles-sync-agent-skills
.fi
.PP
The last command refreshes only eligible image-managed Antigravity
skills from the image catalog; it will not overwrite local edits.
Treat this man page as documentation, not as an executable skill
manager. For invocation details, consult each SKILL.md and the
installed agent's own skill-discovery interface.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If a skill exists in the Git checkout but not in Codex, check the
actual published image revision and whether the container was
recreated. A persistent outer container retains its original
image. If a skill does not update in Antigravity, check for a
locally edited skill or conflicting user-owned path; the sync
script deliberately preserves them.
.PP
When a skill requires external CLI tools, network access or GitHub
authentication, consult its SKILL.md before using it. Having the
skill instructions installed does not itself grant those permissions.
.SH MAINTENANCE
On adding, removing or renaming a directory under
containers/dev-dotfiles-debian/agent-skills, update this catalog,
the corresponding SKILL.md metadata and the agent-skills test.
Avoid duplicating the complete SKILL.md here.
.SH SEE ALSO
dotfiles-ci(7), run-dev-podman.sh(1), run-dev-docker.sh(1)
